ite_memory and a screenshot in which the HUD shows the value you wrote (the HUD redraws a number when the game changes it, so make the game change it after your write if the display does not follow at once).\"\n\nSo I need: write value → game changes it → HUD shows my value (+ change).\n\nFor the coin: write $07EE = 7, then collect a coin → $07EE becomes 8 → HUD shows 08. Proves.\nFor the score: write $07E1 = 9, then gain 100 (stomp) → hundreds digit 9+1=0 with carry → score 001000 → HUD 001000. Proves $07E1 if the carry shows.\n\nBut I already wrote $07E1=9. Now if I collect a coin (+200), score 900+200=1100 → HUD 001100. The hundreds digit would be... 1100: thousands=1, hundreds=1. So $07E1 would go 9→1 (with carry to $07E0). Interesting.\n\nOK let me just get to a coin.\n\nLet me find ? blocks via read_nametable across NT1 rows 16-19, cols 0-15.\n\nActually, better: use find_unused_tiles? No.\n\nLet me read NT1 rows 16,17,18,19, cols 0-15 (x=0,width=16,height=4).\n\nHmm, but NT1 shows level x 256-511. Camera 206 → visible screen x 0-255 = level 206-461 → NT1 cols (206-256)/8 negative... so screen x 0-49 is NT0, 50-255 is NT1. Ugh, mixed nametables.\n\nLet me just read NT1 cols 0-15 rows 16-19.\n\nActually, simpler: get_tile_at_pixel over a grid to find ? blocks. Let me sample y=148 at x=20,40,60,80,100,120,140,160,180,200,220,240. That's a lot of calls.\n\nAlternatively, use the screenshot more carefully. Let me re-screenshot and carefully note the ? block positions, then get_tile_at_pixel there.\n\nActually, I just took a screenshot (after writing): it shows:\n- ? block at approx (180,75) high\n- ? block at approx (85,145)\n- used/blue block at (250,145)? Actually there's a big blue-ish structure at the right edge (x~245-256, y~145-200) which is a pipe or wall.\n\nHmm, and Mario at (250,185).\n\nWait, the \"200\" popup at (180,105). And a ? block at (180,75)? That might actually be at (180,128)? \n\nI clearly can't trust my visual y estimates. Let me get_tile_at