mm, but earlier Mario at low 157 with camera 206 → I assumed abs 413 (page1). Is page 1? Let me read $006D. Earlier I wrote it to 1 and it may have stayed. Actually after the death/restart, page resets. Let me just read $006D.\n\nUgh. Let me simplify: Mario is at screen 207. The unused ? block is at screen 130-145. So move left ~70px. Walking left ~1.5px/frame → ~47 frames. Then jump.\n\nLet me do: play left 40 frames, screenshot, check position.\n\nBut the Goomba! It's around screen 95 moving left, away from Mario if Mario goes left... actually the Goomba moves left (away). So no collision if Mario chases. But Mario might catch up. Let's go.\n\nActually, let me first write $07EE=7 again (it may have been reset? no, coin=2, I wrote 7). Wait, I wrote $07EE=7 earlier; the HUD still shows 02 (stale). If I now collect a coin, $07EE 7→8, HUD→08. \n\nBut careful: if $07EE was overwritten by the game (e.g., the coin count variable), writing 7 and then collecting 1 coin → 8. Good.\n\nBut wait — is $07EE really the coin count? If it's not, collecting a coin would leave my 7 there and the real coin byte would go 2→3, HUD shows 03. Then $07EE would be wrong. We'll see.\n\nLet me also keep $07E1=9 written (score hundreds = 9). Then collecting a coin (+200) → 900+200 = 1100 → HUD 001100.\n\nSo after collecting the next coin, if HUD shows coin 08 and score 001100, both proven!\n\nLet me move left to the unused ? block and jump.\n\nActually, note: I wrote $07E1=9 while the score display was 000400. If $07E1 is the hundreds digit, RAM score = 000900. Then +200 = 001100.\n\nLet me go. Move left 45 frames, screenshot."}
