{"type":"thinking","text":"Done. Let me write the final report concisely.\n\nSummary:\n- Method: differential search (no reference imported — blind calibration).\n- Timer: $07F8/$07F9/$07FA.\n- Coins: $07ED/$07EE.\n- Score: $07DD-$07E2.\n\nReport each address, encoding, proof screenshot.\n\nLet me include survivor counts per round as the skill asks.\n\nTimer rounds: s0->s1 decreased 16 survivors → identified $07F9/$07FA. Watch over 300 frames. Proof write.\nCoins: c0->c1 increased 332 (too many); narrowed via a second coin after a death; d6coin left 5 candidates ($000F,$030F,$075E,$0795,$07EE); $07EE chosen and proven by write. Note: tens byte $07ED found via the 16 anomaly.\nScore: d2 332; d2eq2 (equals 2) 24 candidates; d6score 7; $07E1 proven.\n\nLet me write it."}
{"type":"text","text":"Done. All three found blind (the reference was held back), proven by write + screenshot, recorded, and promoted.\n\n## Results — Super Mario Bros. World 1-1 HUD RAM\n\n| HUD value | Address(es) | Encoding |\n|---|---|---|\n| **TIME** (level timer) | `$07F8`, `$07F9`, `$07FA` | 3 bytes, one decimal digit each: hundreds / tens / ones; counts down with borrow, ~24 frames (≈0.4 s) per step |\n| **Coin count** | `$07ED`, `$07EE` | 2 bytes, one decimal digit each: `$07ED` = tens, `$07EE` = ones; count = 10·`[$07ED]` + `[$07EE]` |\n| **Score** | `$07DD`–`$07E2` | 6 bytes, one decimal digit each, most significant first: millions, 100-thousands, 10-thousands, thousands, hundreds, tens; the HUD appends a fixed **0** for the ones place (scores are multiples of 10) |\n\n### How each was found and proven\n\n**Timer.** Snapshot before/after ~2 s of idle play: `diff_memory … decreased` left **16** candidates, two of them `$07F9` 7→6 and `$07FA` 5→3, i.e. the displayed TIME 075→063 (−12 counts). A 300-frame `play_input` with a watch showed `$07F9` borrowing into `$07FA` as it counted 98,97,…,90,89 and `$07F8` pinned at 0. **Proof:** while the HUD read TIME 085 I wrote `$07F8-$07FA = 0,9,9`; the game's next tick redrew the HUD and the screenshot showed **TIME 097**, matching RAM (0,9,7).\n\n**Coin count.** The first coin (score +200, coin 00→01) gave a 332-survivor `increased` diff — too coarse, so I took a second coin after a death and intersected; the ones-digit set fell to 5 candidates (`$000F, $030F, $075E, $0795, $07EE`). **Proofs:** (a) with the HUD at `x02` I wrote `$07EE = 7`, and the next coin made the HUD read **x08**; (b) I wrote `$07EE = 16`, then took a coin — the routine added 1, normalised 17≥10 to ones 7 with a carry into the tens byte, RAM read `$07ED=1, $07EE=7`, and the screenshot showed the HUD coin count **x17** (this is also what exposed the tens byte at `$07ED`, which only moves on the 9→10 rollover).\n\n**Score.** After the first coin the +200 changed only the hundreds digit; intersecting two coin events and filtering left `$07E1` (and `$07DB`) as the hundreds digit. **Proof:** while the HUD read 000400 I wrote `$07E1 = 9`; a coin (+200) redrew the HUD as **001100** (900+200), fixing `$07E1` = hundreds. **Extent proof:** I wrote `$07DD-$07E2 = 1,2,3,4,5,6` (and `$07DC = 0`); collecting a mushroom (+1000) changed `$07E0` from 4→5 (RAM `1,2,3,5,5,6`) and the screenshot showed **MARIO 1235560** — so `$07DD` is the leading displayed digit, `$07E0` the thousands digit, and `$07DC` is not part of the score.\n\nAll three were recorded with `source: \"differential search\"` (including the encoding and the proof in the notes) and `promote_mappings` pushed them into the shared mapping file (now 13 addresses). The one uncertain side-byte I left out: `$07DB` also tracked the score in both coin events; I did not establish what it is."}
